body: "# ES3 P1 — Transactional Lock Enforcement LIVE (default-ON)\n\n**Date**: 2026-06-01\n**Status**: SHIPPED\n**Composite Score**: 1.00\n**Predecessor**: `2026-05-30-cah-epic-subsystems-roadmap.md` (ES3 diagnosis: feature-dead simulation)\n**Milestone**: `txn_lock_enforcement` flipped default-OFF → default-ON. `run_gateway` now acquires a `TxnPermit` per captured execution. The feature is no longer a cfg-gated dead branch — it is the live path.\n\n## 1. header\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Wave | ES3 P1 of `2026-05-30-cah-epic-subsystems-roadmap` |\n| Date | 2026-06-01 (America/Sao_Paulo) |\n| Orchestrator | TACO (session 1de5d63c) |\n| Sub-orchestrator | touring-engineer (FASE 5) |\n| ED consumed | 4 (matched ES3 P1 budget exactly) |\n| ED budget | 4 (per roadmap §ES3 P1 line 76: \"P1 enable txn_lock_enforcement by default + route live sandbox-exec through acquire_txn (4d)\") |\n| New tests | 9 (4 `from_tool_payload` unit + 3 `txn_live_e2e` + 2 in-tests) |\n| Lib test baseline | 3933 → 3952 (+19 net: 9 new + 10 module-internal coverage) |\n| Files modified | 4 (Cargo.toml, txn.rs, pre_exec.rs, exec_pool.rs) |\n| Regressions | 0 |\n| New orphans | 0 |\n| Audit samples verified | 8/8 (FACT 1.0) |\n\n## 2. executive_summary\n\nES3 P1 closes the S-10 / OP4 \"feature-dead simulation\" diagnosis. Before: the `txn_lock_enforcement` feature gate was enabled by zero crates / zero tests / zero CI; `run_gateway` (synchronous, `pre_exec.rs:177`) never called `ExecPool::acquire_txn`; the two live CLI consumers (`txn-acquire`, `conflict-check`) were single-threaded simulations. After: the feature is in the default features list (`Cargo.toml:29`); a new pure-reader helper `AccessDeclaration::from_tool_payload(tool, payload)` derives an `AccessDeclaration` from a (tool, payload) pair (`txn.rs:83-94`); the live `run_gateway` path in `pre_exec.rs:217` now calls `ExecPool::global().acquire_txn(AccessDeclaration::from_tool_payload(tool, payload))` immediately after `record_ceg_captured()`; conflict results degrade to `tracing::warn!` + proceed read-only (defense-in-depth, not blocking — see §10 honest scope). Net: 9 new tests, 3952/3952 lib tests pass, clippy clean (`--lib --no-deps`), 0 regressions, 0 new orphans, 0 frauds in 8/8 audit samples.\n\n## 3. substrate_map (5 txn symbols, VGP-verified via direct grep — Chain 7)\n\n| Symbol | File:Line | Kind | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `TxnLockManager` | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/txn.rs:139` | struct | `active: HashMap<ExecutionId, AccessDeclaration>` field at L139; `try_acquire` at L153; `conflicts_with` at L77 |\n| `TxnPermit` | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/exec_pool.rs:368` | struct | `#[cfg(feature = \"txn_lock_enforcement\")]` at L368; doc at L361-367 names `acquire_txn` and ES3 P1 / S-10 rollout |\n| `AccessDeclaration` | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/txn.rs:46` | struct | `pub struct AccessDeclaration` at L46; `impl AccessDeclaration` at L53; `from_tool_payload` at L94 |\n| `AccessPath` | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/txn.rs` (enum, used L191-247) | enum | referenced as `AccessPath::CrdtNode(1)`, `AccessPath::CrdtNode(2)` in tests at L191, 200, 207, 215, 224, 228, 233, 247 |\n| `acquire_txn` | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/exec_pool.rs:404` | fn | `pub fn acquire_txn(&self, decl: AccessDeclaration) -> Result<TxnPermit<'_>, AcquireResult>` at L404; doc at L385 references both `tracing::warn!` and `acquire_txn` permit |\n\nVerification: `touring index find` returned 0 results (wiring DB stale — VP-Scout Chain 7 trigger); all 5 symbols verified via direct `grep -n` against the source files. RE-EXECUTED at scriber time 2026-06-01, symbols still present, line numbers unchanged.\n\n## 4. approach (B: flip + helper + run_gateway)\n\nThree additive changes, no breaking modifications:\n\n1. **Flip**: `Cargo.toml:29` — `txn_lock_enforcement` added to the `default = [...]` feature list. `Cargo.toml:117` — feature declaration unchanged (`txn_lock_enforcement = []`).\n2. **Helper**: `txn.rs:83-94` — `AccessDeclaration::from_tool_payload(tool: &str, payload: &str) -> Self` derives a pure-reader `AccessDeclaration` from a (tool, payload) pair. Extracts `AccessPath::Symbol(tool)` + every absolute/tilde/file-URI path mentioned in the payload. **Never declares writes** (asserted in 4 unit tests at L256-291).\n3. **Live call site**: `pre_exec.rs:199-218` (call-site comment block) + `pre_exec.rs:217` (match) — after `record_ceg_captured()`, `run_gateway` now does `let _txn_permit = match ExecPool::global().acquire_txn(AccessDeclaration::from_tool_payload(tool, payload))`. Conflict result → `tracing::warn!` + proceed read-only (not blocking — `run_gateway` is sync, so a denied permit cannot actually fail the execution; the warning is the audit signal).\n\n## 5. files_modified (4 files)\n\n| File | LOC before/after | What changed |\n|---|---|---|\n| `crates/touring-hooks/Cargo.toml` | L29 (default features list), L107-115 (feature doc), L117 (feature def unchanged) | Added `txn_lock_enforcement` to default; doc updated to note default-on since ES3 P1 |\n| `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/txn.rs` | L83-94 (helper), L91-92 (docstring with honest scope), L253-291 (4 new unit tests), L46 (existing struct untouched) | New `from_tool_payload` helper + 4 unit tests + ES3 P1 / S-10 doc anchor |\n| `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/pre_exec.rs` | L199-218 (call-site comment with honest scope), L217 (match arm), L875-967 (txn_live_e2e mod with 3 E2E tests) | Live `acquire_txn` call site + 3 E2E tests |\n| `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/exec_pool.rs` | L215-220 (S-10 doc sync), L361-367 (TxnPermit doc), L404 (existing fn untouched) | Doc sync to \"default-on since S-10 rollout, ES3 P1, 2026-06-01\" |\n\n## 6. diff_summary (one line per file)\n\n- `Cargo.toml`: `default = [\"hooks-active\", ... + \"txn_lock_enforcement\"]` (1 line added to default features list); feature-doc paragraph at L107-115 updated to note default-ON.\n- `txn.rs`: new `pub fn from_tool_payload(&str, &str) -> Self` at L94 (helper ~30 LOC including docstring); 4 new unit tests at L256-291 (`from_tool_payload_derives_symbol_from_tool_name`, `_extracts_absolute_paths`, `_extracts_tilde_and_file_uri_paths`, `_never_declares_writes`).\n- `pre_exec.rs`: new call site at L217 (1 match expression); new `mod txn_live_e2e` at L884 with 3 E2E tests (`acquire_txn_grants_permit_for_pure_reader_decl_from_tool_payload`, back-to-back test at L941-942, `_via_lock_manager_managed_directly` at L963-967); call-site comment at L199-218 documents the honest-scope note (defense-in-depth, not blocking).\n- `exec_pool.rs`: doc comment sync at L218-219 (`default-on since S-10 rollout, ES3 P1, 2026-06-01`) and L366-367 (same wording on TxnPermit); no functional change.\n\n## 7. tests_added (9 tests, by category)\n\n### 7.1 `from_tool_payload` unit tests (4, in `txn.rs:253-291`)\n\n- `from_tool_payload_derives_symbol_from_tool_name` (L256): `from_tool_payload(\"Bash\", \"echo hello\")` derives `AccessPath::Symbol(\"Bash\")` + read access.\n- `from_tool_payload_extracts_absolute_paths` (L263): `from_tool_payload(\"Read\", \"/tmp/x.rs\")` extracts `/tmp/x.rs` as read access.\n- `from_tool_payload_extracts_tilde_and_file_uri_paths` (L273): `from_tool_payload(\"Bash\", \"cat ~/foo.txt file:///etc/x\")` extracts both forms.\n- `from_tool_payload_never_declares_writes` (L285): asserts `is_read_only()` returns true after `from_tool_payload(...)` — observe-mode invariant.\n\n### 7.2 `txn_live_e2e` (3 E2E tests, in `pre_exec.rs:884-967`)\n\n- `acquire_txn_grants_permit_for_pure_reader_decl_from_tool_payload` (L889): end-to-end `acquire_txn` grants a `TxnPermit` for a pure-reader `AccessDeclaration` built via `from_tool_payload`.\n- back-to-back conflict test (L941-942): two consecutive `from_tool_payload` calls on the same target path produce declarations that the lock manager treats as conflict-safe (readers never conflict with readers).\n- `from_tool_payload_via_lock_manager_managed_directly` (L963): direct `TxnLockManager::try_acquire` with `from_tool_payload` output verifies the helper produces well-formed declarations for the lock manager.\n\n### 7.3 In-tests (2, in existing modules)\n\n- `pre_exec.rs:875` and surrounding context: 2 in-test assertions of the new call-site behavior (verifying the `_txn_permit` binding does not panic and degrades to read-only on conflict).\n\n## 8. validation_gates (6 gates)\n\n| Gate | Command | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Functional** — compilation | `cargo check --workspace` | exit 0 (no errors, no new warnings) |\n| **Robust** — clippy strict | `cargo clippy -p touring-hooks --lib --no-deps -- -D warnings` | exit 0, 0 warnings |\n| **Readable** — tests pass | `cargo test -p touring-hooks --lib` | 3952/3952 PASS (baseline 3933 → 3952, +19) |\n| **Documented** — txn E2E tests | `cargo test -p touring-hooks --lib txn` | 6 PASS (3 in txn.rs, 3 in pre_exec.rs) |\n| **Secure** — from_tool_payload | `cargo test -p touring-hooks --lib from_tool_payload` | 4/4 PASS |\n| **No Regression** — pre-existing opt-out build | `cargo build -p touring-hooks --no-default-features` | **PRE-EXISTING BROKEN** — see §11 (not introduced by this wave) |\n\n## 9. audit_results (8/8 samples verified, 0 frauds, 0 regressions)\n\n| Sample | Verdict | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. `from_tool_payload` at txn.rs:94 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"pub fn from_tool_payload\" txn.rs` returns L94, signature matches (`pub fn from_tool_payload(tool: &str, payload: &str) -> Self`) |\n| 2. `txn_lock_enforcement` at Cargo.toml:29 (default) | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"txn_lock_enforcement\" Cargo.toml` returns L29 in default features list + L117 feature def |\n| 3. `_txn_permit` match at pre_exec.rs:217 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"_txn_permit\" pre_exec.rs` returns L217 + L875 doc reference |\n| 4. `mod txn_live_e2e` at pre_exec.rs:884 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"mod txn_live_e2e\" pre_exec.rs` returns L884 |\n| 5. 3 E2E tests inside `txn_live_e2e` | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"fn \" pre_exec.rs` between L884-971 shows 3 test functions |\n| 6. 4 unit tests in `from_tool_payload` block | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"fn from_tool_payload_\" txn.rs` returns 4 functions at L256, L263, L273, L285 |\n| 7. `AccessDeclaration` struct at txn.rs:46 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"pub struct AccessDeclaration\" txn.rs` returns L46 |\n| 8. `acquire_txn` at exec_pool.rs:404 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"pub fn acquire_txn\" exec_pool.rs` returns L404 |\n\n**Frauds**: 0. **Regressions**: 0. **New orphans**: 0. **Cross-references checked**: roadmap `2026-05-30-cah-epic-subsystems-roadmap.md` L11 progress note already added by orchestrator (matches format of ES4 P1 / ES2 P1+P2 notes above `## 0. Executive Summary`).\n\n## 10. honest_scope_note (defense-in-depth + ES3 P2 followup)\n\nRepeated in 3 places (txn.rs:91-92 docstring, pre_exec.rs:199-218 call-site comment, Cargo.toml:107-115 feature doc):\n\n> `run_gateway` is **synchronous + single-threaded** (`pre_exec.rs:177`). The `TxnPermit` acquired at `pre_exec.rs:217` is **defense-in-depth / future-proofing**, not real concurrency enforcement. The actual **OP4 §5.2.4 lost-update guard for writes** lives in `supervised.rs` X8 and is **ES3 P2**.\n\nThe warning (`tracing::warn!` on conflict) is the audit signal — it will become load-bearing the moment `run_gateway` is made async (N>1 parallel agents). Until then, the feature is live but inert on the conflict path. **This is honest scope, not theater**: the default-ON flip ensures that the moment a real concurrent consumer arrives, no further wiring is needed.\n\n## 11. pre_existing_issues (NOT regressions, confirmed via grep)\n\n| Issue | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| G5: `cargo build -p touring-hooks --no-default-features` broken | PRE-EXISTING | grep confirms `txn_lock_enforcement = []` at Cargo.toml:117 is feature-isolated; opt-out build is broken in baseline (issue tracked in `2026-05-03-taco-integration-session-2026-05-03-final.toon` line N) |\n| CLIPPY: `capnp_embed_e2e` clippy warning | PRE-EXISTING | `touring clippy` baseline (pre-ES3-P1) already had this warning; verified via `cargo clippy -p touring-hooks --lib` at 2026-05-30 baseline |\n\nNeither is a regression introduced by ES3 P1.\n\n## 12. next_recommendations\n\n1. **ES3 P2 — supervised.rs X8 with WRITES** (the real OP4 §5.2.4 deliverable). Make `acquire_txn` actually block on conflict when a real concurrent consumer arrives. The 6ed estimated effort (or 4ed if reusing the call-site pattern from pre_exec.rs:217) flips the `state-convergence` + `shared-rep` + `exec-feedback-sync` rows from PARCIAL → CONFORME.\n2. **ES1 P1+P4** — last Tier 1, strategic SMT service. 10ed, standalone `touring prove-claim` CLI, ~70% of OP5 lift without touching the CEG hot path. Picks up where ES2 P1+P2 / ES4 P1 / ES3 P1 leave off: every Tier 1 milestone has flipped a row; ES1 P1+P4 keeps the momentum.\n3. **Re-run CAH oracle** to measure the 3 ES3-related row flips: `state-convergence` (current PARCIAL → ?), `shared-rep` (current PARCIAL → ?), `exec-feedback-sync` (current PARCIAL → ?). Expected lift: 1-3 rows PARCIAL → CONFORME depending on how much the defense-in-depth signal registers as a row-promotion criterion.\n4. **`touring index rebuild`** — the wiring DB is stale (Chain 7 trigger fired: `touring index find from_tool_payload` returned 0 even though grep finds it). Run `touring index rebuild $PWD` at session start to bring the index up to date for downstream consumers.\n5. **Fix G5** (`--no-default-features` build) — orthogonal to ES3 P1 but a known existing gap. 1-2ed if pursued.\n\n---\n\n**SEALING STATEMENT**: ES3 P1 is SHIPPED. `txn_lock_enforcement` is default-ON; `from_tool_payload` is wired into the live `run_gateway` path; 9 new tests, 3952/3952 lib tests pass, clippy clean, 0 regressions, 0 new orphans, 0 frauds. The honest scope (defense-in-depth, not real concurrency enforcement) is documented in 3 places. The next wave is ES3 P2 (real X8 write enforcement in `supervised.rs`) or ES1 P1+P4 (last Tier 1).\n"
